// toList
List<String> names = users.stream().map(User::getName).collect(Collectors.toList());

// toSet — deduplicates
Set<String> uniqueRoles = users.stream().map(User::getRole).collect(Collectors.toSet());

// joining — concatenate strings
String csv = names.stream().collect(Collectors.joining(", "));

// groupingBy — group by role
Map<String, List<User>> byRole = users.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(User::getRole));

// toMap — key=name, value=user
Map<String, User> byName = users.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.toMap(User::getName, u -> u));
```

```java
List<Integer> nums = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);

// With identity (initial value) — returns T
int sum = nums.stream().reduce(0, Integer::sum); // 15
int product = nums.stream().reduce(1, (a, b) -> a * b); // 120

// Without identity — returns Optional<T>
Optional<Integer> max = nums.stream().reduce(Integer::max);
max.ifPresent(System.out::println); // 5
```

